WEBVTT

00:00:02.484 --> 00:00:04.514
Okay, so let me show you something.

00:00:04.564 --> 00:00:05.794
You know flashcards?

00:00:05.844 --> 00:00:08.104
Question on the front, answer on the back.

00:00:08.124 --> 00:00:10.624
You quiz yourself, and the app brings each card

00:00:10.644 --> 00:00:12.314
back right before you'd forget it.

00:00:12.973 --> 00:00:14.393
You tell it how well you knew it,

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:16.580
and that decides when you see it again.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.803
And honestly, that part works great.

00:00:19.843 --> 00:00:23.233
Thing is, a card is basically just text.

00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:25.353
And most of what we actually learn...

00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:26.303
isn't.

00:00:26.323 --> 00:00:27.103
So...

00:00:27.123 --> 00:00:29.193
what if a card could be anything?

00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:30.913
Like, learning chess?

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:33.113
Find the checkmate, right there on the board.

00:00:33.477 --> 00:00:34.227
Piano?

00:00:34.277 --> 00:00:36.440
Play the chord it asks for.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.480
Japanese?

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.000
Draw the character with your finger,

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.757
and the AI tells you how your strokes look.

00:00:41.777 --> 00:00:42.917
Got a coding interview?

00:00:42.937 --> 00:00:45.197
Solve the problem, and the tests run the second

00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:46.663
you hit check.

00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:47.583
Chemistry?

00:00:47.603 --> 00:00:49.065
Balance the equation.

00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:51.025
Math gives you new numbers every time,

00:00:51.045 --> 00:00:53.385
so you end up learning how it works.

00:00:53.475 --> 00:00:54.095
History?

00:00:54.115 --> 00:00:56.628
Put the events in order on a timeline.

00:00:56.648 --> 00:00:57.628
Ear training?

00:00:57.648 --> 00:00:59.668
Listen to two notes and say how far apart

00:00:59.688 --> 00:01:01.004
they are.

00:01:01.024 --> 00:01:02.044
Even trivia:

00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:03.524
how many times does your heart beat in a

00:01:03.544 --> 00:01:04.494
lifetime?

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:20.074
And all of it runs on FSRS,

00:01:20.094 --> 00:01:22.394
the same scheduler modern Anki uses,

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:24.644
so every card comes back right when you need

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:25.061
it.

00:01:25.081 --> 00:01:26.741
Your decks show what's due today.

00:01:26.761 --> 00:01:29.354
And the stats show how much you actually remember,

00:01:29.374 --> 00:01:30.804
and what's about to slip.

00:01:33.178 --> 00:01:35.321
And it's built to work really well with AI

00:01:35.341 --> 00:01:36.174
agents.

00:01:36.194 --> 00:01:38.241
You don't need one, most cards are checked by

00:01:38.261 --> 00:01:39.331
little scripts right on your

00:01:39.621 --> 00:01:40.121
computer.

00:01:40.141 --> 00:01:41.214
But if you have one,

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.161
it can do everything you can:

00:01:43.181 --> 00:01:45.041
turn your lecture notes into cards,

00:01:45.061 --> 00:01:47.801
grade your explanations, read your stats and tell you

00:01:47.821 --> 00:01:49.241
what to review next.

00:01:49.261 --> 00:01:52.401
Sign in with ChatGPT, bring your own API key,

00:01:52.421 --> 00:01:54.081
or just let your agent drive it from the

00:01:54.101 --> 00:01:54.931
command line.

00:01:56.484 --> 00:01:58.314
And this is my favorite part.

00:01:58.404 --> 00:02:00.704
Every card is a little program you can open

00:02:00.724 --> 00:02:01.877
and change.

00:02:01.897 --> 00:02:03.344
Or just ask your agent:

00:02:03.364 --> 00:02:05.424
make me a card that teaches Morse code.

00:02:05.444 --> 00:02:07.344
A minute later, it's in your deck.

00:02:07.364 --> 00:02:11.064
Oh, and you can change the whole look,

00:02:11.084 --> 00:02:13.664
or grab decks, themes and card types other people

00:02:13.684 --> 00:02:15.034
made, right from the market.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.040
It's called Etude.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.830
It's free, it's open source,

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:22.950
and it's on GitHub.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:23.840
Go try it.
